  "prediction": "**Summary of the Report: Foreign Currency Budget Rates and Management at the Department of Defense**\n\nThe Department of Defense (DOD) establishes foreign currency budget rates to determine its funding needs for overseas expenditures. These rates are used to calculate gains or losses due to foreign currency fluctuations. The report examines DOD's revised foreign currency budget rates since 2009 and their relationship to DOD's projected Operation and Maintenance (O&M) and Military Personnel (MILPERS) funding needs.\n\n**Key Findings:**\n\n1. DOD revised its foreign currency budget rates in fiscal years 2014-2016 to more closely align with market rates, resulting in decreased projected O&M and MILPERS funding needs.\n2. The revised budget rates also decreased potential gains and losses in the amount of funds available for planned overseas expenditures.\n3. DOD's use of revised foreign currency budget rates resulted in a decrease of $2.7 billion in projected funding needs from fiscal years 2009-2017.\n4. The report highlights issues with data accuracy and completeness in DOD's financial reporting on foreign currency gains and losses, which hinders effective management of the Foreign Currency Fluctuations, Defense (FCFD) account.\n5. The Army's accounting system charges disbursements to the current fiscal year appropriation instead of the fiscal year appropriation that incurred the obligation, resulting in inaccurate data.\n\n**Recommendations:**\n\n1. The Under Secretary of Defense (Comptroller) should conduct a review of foreign currency rates used at disbursement to determine cost-saving opportunities.\n2. The Under Secretary of Defense (Comptroller) should analyze realized and projected losses to determine the necessary size of the FCFD account balance.\n3. The Under Secretary of Defense (Comptroller) should revise the Financial Management Regulation to include guidance on ensuring data completeness and accuracy.\n4. The Secretary of the Army should develop a plan with timelines for implementing changes to its General Fund Enterprise Business System to accurately record disbursements.\n\n**Conclusion:**\n\nThe report highlights the importance of accurate and complete data in managing foreign currency gains and losses at DOD. The recommendations aim to improve the management of the FCFD account and ensure that DOD has the necessary information to make informed decisions about its foreign currency budget rates.",
